From 9dd408b8ee85eec4491ce7176dc50dd7c87afe22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <daniel@Daniels-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:46:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve generated token provenance in DeepSeek V4.1 complete
 responses

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354; applied after the
198-patch 1022 attention stack (dea96d04ea9e).

The delegating non-streaming path discarded generated token IDs between
reasoning and tool extraction. Literal EOS spellings in ordinary text and
tool arguments were consequently removed. Use the matching reasoning
engine for one token-aware pass; retain the existing streaming adapters,
JSON forced-tool conversion and mixed-parser routing.

Quality: preserves literal arguments without changing weights, sampling,
steering arithmetic, true special-token removal or the input encoder.
Tests: 19 new regressions fail on both retained r6x and unmodified 1022;
all 4375 parser-engine tests pass with this patch in the candidate image
using CPU only. GPU requests remain to be qualified.
Upstream status: downstream maintenance fix; not submitted upstream.
